gine/godot/labels/topic:export","name":"topic:export","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-07-20T02:48:29Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T18:33:19Z","closed_at":"2025-07-20T18:32:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot_v4.4.1-stable_win64\n\n### System information\n\nwindows11 - Godot_v4.4.1-stable_win64\n\n### Issue description\n\nDuring the packaging process of my WebGL project, I encountered an issue with excessively large PCK package size. For instance, if the project contains 30 levels (scenes) and each level’s resources are approximately 5MB in size, the total volume of the PCK package will reach 150MB or even larger. This not only imposes pressure on network transmission but also reduces the game’s loading speed.\n\nIn this regard, I have two questions:\n\nIs it possible to implement dynamic loading for levels? That is, loading the resources corresponding to the current level only when the player enters it.\nIf Level A and Level B share models or files, is there a way to avoid reloading these shared resources to further optimize the package size?\n\n<img width=\"2559\" height=\"1438\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d82cbbba-8170-42ab-af15-20f8974e13f3\" />\nThe Godot engine can run 1GB of pck files in the WebGL environment. Although it is running locally and there are some audio issues, I still think it's amazing.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n-\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n-","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co